AB  - Information entropy tools are increasingly used to quantify uncertainty, dependence and information transfer in water system management (WSM), but proliferating indices make applications difficult to compare. This paper reviewed entropy-related WSM studies in the Web of Science Collection. The search string (“information entropy” OR “mutual information” OR “transfer entropy” OR “maximum entropy” OR “entropy weight method” OR “sample entropy” OR “water quality entropy”) AND “water” yielded 6039 unique records; 5645 records published during 1981-2025 were analyzed, and 2890 WSM-relevant papers were selected by title/abstract/source screening and classified by water body and management scenario. We synthesize univariate uncertainty, multivariate dependence, entropy-weighting and optimization methods across data analysis, modelling, forecasting/risk assessment, water-quality analysis and source identification in different waterbodies. The review provides a scenario-oriented taxonomy to help users select appropriate indices and improve reproducibility and practical precision in entropy-based WSM, leading future directions in the era of big data and digital water.
