AB  - The U.S. Forest Inventory and Analysis (FIA) database provides comprehensive forest information on composition, structure, biomass, growth, removals, mortality, and disturbance. However, its complex data structure and design-based estimation framework can limit use by individuals without programming, database, or survey-estimation expertise. We developed FIALab, a free, cross-platform desktop application that provides an interactive environment for FIA data analysis without requiring software installation or coding. Seven modules support plot-level analysis of forest structure, composition, and biomass, point mapping of plot attributes, wall-to-wall interpolation, tree growth and allometry, forest health and disturbance assessment, climate-data acquisition and climate-forest analysis, and design-based forest carbon estimation. We demonstrate FIALab using statewide FIA data from Maine, USA, and evaluate broader applicability with data from Georgia. FIALab integrates data processing, statistical estimation, visualization, and spatial analysis, thereby reducing technical barriers and expanding the use of FIA data in forest management, research, education, and resource planning.
